</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A simplified method to design suspended cabs for counterbalance trucks</article-title><source>Journal of Sound and Vibration</source><year>2002</year><volume>253</volume><fpage>283</fpage><lpage>293</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/jsvi.2001.4260</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patil</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Palanichamy</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A mathematical model of tractor-occupant system with a new seat suspension for minimization of vibration response</article-title><source>Applied Mathematical Modelling</source><year>1988</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>63</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0307-904X(88)90024-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hansson</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Optimization of agricultural tractor cab suspension using the evolution method</article-title><source>Computers and Electronics in Agriculture</source><year>1995</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>35</fpage><lpage>49</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0168-1699(94)00036-P</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hansson</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>PM&#x02013;Power and machinery: working space requirement for an agricultural tractor axle suspension</article-title><source>Biosystems Engineering</source><year>2002</year><volume>81</volume><fpage>57</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/bioe.2001.0007</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author